--
-- Positions: Claude (Opus 5.5) read them from the relief against the written accounts,
-- which give them in words only, so every look is made "within" a distance:
--   Raglan "on an elevated spur of the Sapoune Heights"
--   Lucan "on rising ground at the near end of the Causeway Heights"
--   the Light Brigade at the west end of the North Valley
--   the Russian battery at the east end, about 2 km on
--   the captured British guns in redoubts on the Causeway Heights crest, and their
--   reverse (south) slope, where the Russians were taking them off
-- Eyes: a man on horseback 2.5 m; guns and gunners 1.5 m.
source Copernicus GLO-30 surface model (today's trees and buildings count as ground), 30 m grid
place raglan 44.5370 33.5760 eye 2.5
place lucan 44.5340 33.6050 eye 2.5
place light-brigade 44.5400 33.6070 eye 2.5
place russian-battery 44.5400 33.6320 eye 1.5
place redoubt-crest-west 44.5340 33.6150 eye 1.5
place redoubt-crest-mid 44.5310 33.6250 eye 1.5
place redoubt-crest-east 44.5280 33.6350 eye 1.5
place reverse-slope-west 44.5325 33.6150 eye 1.5
place reverse-slope-mid 44.5295 33.6250 eye 1.5
place reverse-slope-east 44.5265 33.6350 eye 1.5
look raglan russian-battery within 300 150
look raglan redoubt-crest-mid within 300 150
look raglan reverse-slope-mid within 300 150
look raglan reverse-slope-east within 300 150
look lucan russian-battery within 300 150
look lucan redoubt-crest-mid within 300 150
look lucan reverse-slope-mid within 300 150
look lucan reverse-slope-east within 300 150
look light-brigade russian-battery within 300 150
look light-brigade reverse-slope-mid within 300 150
look light-brigade reverse-slope-east within 300 150
